|                             src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg/250px-Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail"
|                             srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg/500px-Tim_Berners-Lee_April_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"
|                             style="--mw-file-upright: 0.75"
|                             width="190"
|                         <figcaption>
|                           id="mwUQ"
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Berners-Lee"
|                             id="mwUg"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Tim Berners-Lee"
|                             "Tim Berners-Lee"
|                           " in April 2009"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwUw"
|                         "In 1980, the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physicist"
|                           id="mwVA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Physicist"
|                           "physicist"
|                         " "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Berners-Lee"
|                           id="mwVQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Tim Berners-Lee"
|                           "Tim Berners-Lee"
|                         ", a contractor at "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CERN"
|                           id="mwVg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="CERN"
|                           "CERN"
|                         ", proposed and prototyped "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ENQUIRE"
|                           id="mwVw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="ENQUIRE"
|                           "ENQUIRE"
|                         ", a system for CERN researchers to use and share documents. In 1989, Berners-Lee wrote a memo proposing an "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet"
|                           id="mwWA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Internet"
|                           "Internet"
|                         "-based "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertext"
|                           id="mwWQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Hypertext"
|                           "hypertext"
|                         " system."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt50"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-5"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-5"
|                             id="mwWg"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwWw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwXA"
|                                 "["
|                               "4"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwXQ"
|                                 "]"
|                         " Berners-Lee specified HTML and wrote the browser and server software in late 1990. That year, Berners-Lee and CERN "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_system"
|                           id="mwXg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Data system"
|                           "data systems"
|                         " engineer "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Cailliau"
|                           id="mwXw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Robert Cailliau"
|                           "Robert Cailliau"
|                         " collaborated on a joint request for funding, but the project was not formally adopted by CERN. In his personal notes of 1990, Berners-Lee listed "some of the many areas in which hypertext is used"; an "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encyclopedia"
|                           id="mwYA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Encyclopedia"
|                           "encyclopedia"
|                         " is the first entry."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt53"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-6"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-6"
|                             id="mwYQ"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwYg"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwYw"
|                                 "["
|                               "5"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwZA"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwZQ"
|                         "The first publicly available description of HTML was a document called "HTML Tags","
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt56"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-7"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-7"
|                             id="mwZg"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwZw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwaA"
|                                 "["
|                               "6"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwaQ"
|                                 "]"
|                         " first mentioned on the Internet by Tim Berners-Lee in late 1991."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt57"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"tagshtml"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-tagshtml_8-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-tagshtml-8"
|                             id="mwag"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwaw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwbA"
|                                 "["
|                               "7"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwbQ"
|                                 "]"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt60"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-9"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-9"
|                             id="mwbg"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwbw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwcA"
|                                 "["
|                               "8"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwcQ"
|                                 "]"
|                         " It describes 18 elements comprising the initial, relatively simple design of HTML. Except for the hyperlink tag, these were strongly influenced by "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CERN_SGML"
|                           id="mwcg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="CERN SGML"
|                           "CERN SGML"
|                         ", an in-house "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_Generalized_Markup_Language"
|                           id="mwcw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Standard Generalized Markup Language"
|                           "Standard Generalized Markup Language"
|                         " (SGML)-based documentation format at CERN. Eleven of these elements still exist in HTML 4."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt63"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-10"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-10"
|                             id="mwdA"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwdQ"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwdg"
|                                 "["
|                               "9"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwdw"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mweA"
|                         "HTML is a "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markup_language"
|                           id="mweQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Markup language"
|                           "markup language"
|                         " that "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser"
|                           id="mweg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Web browser"
|                           "web browsers"
|                         " use to interpret and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typesetting"
|                           id="mwew"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Typesetting"
|                           "compose"
|                         " text, images, and other material into visible or audible web pages. Default characteristics for every item of HTML markup are defined in the browser, and these characteristics can be altered or enhanced by the web page designer's additional use of "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS"
|                           id="mwfA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="CSS"
|                           "CSS"
|                         ". Many of the text elements are mentioned in the 1988 ISO technical report TR 9537 "
|                         <i>
|                           id="mwfQ"
|                           "Techniques for using SGML"
|                         ", which describes the features of early text formatting languages such as that used by the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TYPSET_and_RUNOFF"
|                           id="mwfg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="TYPSET and RUNOFF"
|                           "RUNOFF command"
|                         " developed in the early 1960s for the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compatible_Time-Sharing_System"
|                           id="mwfw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Compatible Time-Sharing System"
|                           "CTSS"
|                         " (Compatible Time-Sharing System) operating system. These formatting commands were derived from the commands used by typesetters to manually format documents. However, the SGML concept of generalized markup is based on elements (nested annotated ranges with attributes) rather than merely print effects, with separate structure and markup. HTML has been progressively moved in this direction with CSS."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwgA"
|                         "Berners-Lee considered HTML to be an application of SGML. It was formally defined as such by the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Engineering_Task_Force"
|                           id="mwgQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Internet Engineering Task Force"
|                           "Internet Engineering Task Force"
|                         " (IETF) with the mid-1993 publication of the first proposal for an HTML specification, the "Hypertext Markup Language (HTML)" "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Draft"
|                           id="mwgg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Internet Draft"
|                           "Internet Draft"
|                         " by Berners-Lee and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Connolly_(computer_scientist)"
|                           id="mwgw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Dan Connolly (computer scientist)"
|                           "Dan Connolly"
|                         ", which included an SGML "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Document_type_definition"
|                           id="mwhA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Document type definition"
|                           "document type definition"
|                         " to define the syntax."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt66"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-11"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-11"
|                             id="mwhQ"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwhg"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwhw"
|                                 "["
|                               "10"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwiA"
|                                 "]"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt69"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-12"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-12"
|                             id="mwiQ"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwig"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwiw"
|                                 "["
|                               "11"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwjA"
|                                 "]"
|                         " The draft expired after six months, but was notable for its acknowledgment of the "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosaic_(web_browser)"
|                           id="mwjQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Mosaic (web browser)"
|                           "NCSA Mosaic"
|                         " browser's custom tag for embedding in-line images, reflecting the IETF's philosophy of basing standards on successful prototypes. Similarly, "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dave_Raggett"
|                           id="mwjg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Dave Raggett"
|                           "Dave Raggett"
|                         "'s competing Internet Draft, "HTML+ (Hypertext Markup Format)", from late 1993, suggested standardizing already-implemented features like tables and fill-out forms."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt72"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"html+"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-html+-13"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-html+_13-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-html+-13"
|                             id="mwjw"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwkA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwkQ"
|                                 "["
|                               "12"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwkg"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwkw"
|                         "After the HTML and HTML+ drafts expired in early 1994, the IETF created an HTML Working Group. In 1995, this working group completed "HTML 2.0", the first HTML specification intended to be treated as a standard against which future implementations should be based."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt73"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":""},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Ref RFC","href":"./Template:Ref_RFC"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1866"},"quote":{"wt":"This document thus defines an HTML 2.0 (to distinguish it from the previous informal specifications). Future (generally upwardly compatible) versions of HTML with new features will be released with higher version numbers."}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           id="cite_ref-14"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-14"
|                             id="mwlA"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwlQ"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwlg"
|                                 "["
|                               "13"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwlw"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwmA"
|                         "Further development under the auspices of the IETF was stalled by competing interests. "
|                         <span>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"As of","href":"./Template:As_of"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"1996"},"since":{"wt":"y"},"post":{"wt":","}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           id="mwmQ"
|                           typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                           "Since 1996"
|                         <span>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           typeof="mw:Nowiki"
|                         <span>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           ","
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update"
|                           style="display:none;"
|                           <a>
|                             class="external text"
|                             data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=HTML&action=edit"
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=HTML&action=edit"
|                             rel="mw:ExtLink"
|                             <span>
|                               typeof="mw:Entity"
|                               "["
|                             "update"
|                             <span>
|                               typeof="mw:Entity"
|                               "]"
|                         <span>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           typeof="mw:Nowiki"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_1996"
|                           rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt82"
|                           href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements"
|                           id="mwmg"
|                           rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                         " the HTML specifications have been maintained, with input from commercial software vendors, by the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Web_Consortium"
|                           id="mwmw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="World Wide Web Consortium"
|                           "World Wide Web Consortium"
|                         " (W3C)."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt85"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"raggett"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-raggett-15"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-raggett_15-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-raggett-15"
|                             id="mwnA"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwnQ"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwng"
|                                 "["
|                               "14"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwnw"
|                                 "]"
|                         " In 2000, HTML became an international standard ("
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Organization_for_Standardization"
|                           id="mwoA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="International Organization for Standardization"
|                           "ISO"
|                         "/"
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Electrotechnical_Commission"
|                           id="mwoQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="International Electrotechnical Commission"
|                           "IEC"
|                         " 15445:2000). HTML 4.01 was published in late 1999, with further errata published through 2001. In 2004, development began on HTML5 in the "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_Hypertext_Application_Technology_Working_Group"
|                           id="mwog"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Web Hypertext Application Technology Working Group"
|                           "Web Hypertext Application Technology Working Group"
|                         " (WHATWG), which became a joint deliverable with the W3C in 2008, and was completed and standardized on 28 October 2014."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt88"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-16"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-16"
|                             id="mwow"
