|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAbQ"
|                                   "["
|                                 "49"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAbU"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAbY"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAbc"
|                           "Although its syntax closely resembles that of "
|                           <a>
|                             class="mw-redirect"
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SGML"
|                             id="mwAbg"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="SGML"
|                             "SGML"
|                           ", "
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML5"
|                             id="mwAbk"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="HTML5"
|                             "HTML5"
|                           " has abandoned any attempt to be an SGML application and has explicitly defined its own "html" serialization, in addition to an alternative XML-based XHTML5 serialization."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt225"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-51"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-51"
|                               id="mwAbo"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAbs"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAbw"
|                                   "["
|                                 "50"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAb0"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAb4"
|                           "2011"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwAb8"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             " "
|                           "HTML5 – Last Call"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAcA"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAcE"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAcI"
|                           "On 14 February 2011, the W3C extended the charter of its HTML Working Group with clear milestones for HTML5. In May 2011, the working group advanced HTML5 to "Last Call", an invitation to communities inside and outside W3C to confirm the technical soundness of the specification. The W3C developed a comprehensive test suite to achieve broad interoperability for the full specification by 2014, which was the target date for recommendation."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt228"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"w3c2014"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-w3c2014-52"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-w3c2014_52-0"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-w3c2014-52"
|                               id="mwAcM"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAcQ"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAcU"
|                                   "["
|                                 "51"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAcY"
|                                   "]"
|                           " In January 2011, the WHATWG renamed its "HTML5" living standard to "HTML". The W3C nevertheless continued its project to release HTML5."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt231"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-53"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-53"
|                               id="mwAcc"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAcg"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAck"
|                                   "["
|                                 "52"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAco"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAcs"
|                           "2012"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwAcw"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             " "
|                           "HTML5 – Candidate Recommendation"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAc0"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAc4"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAc8"
|                           "In July 2012, WHATWG and "
|                           <a>
|                             class="mw-redirect"
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W3C"
|                             id="mwAdA"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="W3C"
|                             "W3C"
|                           " decided on a degree of separation. W3C will continue the HTML5 specification work, focusing on a single definitive standard, which is considered a "snapshot" by WHATWG. The WHATWG organization will continue its work with HTML5 as a "Living Standard". The concept of a living standard is that it is never complete and is always being updated and improved. New features can be added but functionality will not be removed."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt234"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-54"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-54"
|                               id="mwAdE"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAdI"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAdM"
|                                   "["
|                                 "53"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAdQ"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAdU"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAdY"
|                           "In December 2012, W3C designated HTML5 as a Candidate Recommendation."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt237"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-55"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-55"
|                               id="mwAdc"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAdg"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAdk"
|                                   "["
|                                 "54"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAdo"
|                                   "]"
|                           " The criterion for advancement to "
|                           <a>
|                             class="mw-redirect"
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W3C_recommendation#W3C_recommendation_(REC)"
|                             id="mwAds"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="W3C recommendation"
|                             "W3C Recommendation"
|                           " is "two 100% complete and fully interoperable implementations"."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt240"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"W3Crec"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-W3Crec-56"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-W3Crec_56-0"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-W3Crec-56"
|                               id="mwAdw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAd0"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAd4"
|                                   "["
|                                 "55"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAd8"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAeA"
|                           "2014"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwAeE"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             " "
|                           "HTML5 – Proposed Recommendation and Recommendation"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAeI"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAeM"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAeQ"
|                           "In September 2014, W3C moved HTML5 to Proposed Recommendation."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt243"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-57"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-57"
|                               id="mwAeU"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAeY"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAec"
|                                   "["
|                                 "56"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAeg"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <dt>
|                           id="mwAek"
|                         <dd>
|                           id="mwAeo"
|                           "On 28 October 2014, HTML5 was released as a stable W3C Recommendation,"
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt246"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-58"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-58"
|                               id="mwAes"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAew"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAe0"
|                                   "["
|                                 "57"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAe4"
|                                   "]"
|                           " meaning the specification process is complete."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt249"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"finalars"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-finalars-59"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-finalars_59-0"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-finalars-59"
|                               id="mwAe8"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAfA"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAfE"
|                                   "["
|                                 "58"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAfI"
|                                   "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <section>
|                         aria-labelledby="XHTML_versions"
|                         data-mw-section-id="9"
|                         id="mwAfM"
|                         <div>
|                           class="mw-heading mw-heading4"
|                           <h4>
|                             id="XHTML_versions"
|                             "XHTML versions"
|                         "
"
|                         <span>
|                           about="#mwt250"
|                           class="mw-empty-elt"
|                           data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"XHTML"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           id="mwAfQ"
|                           typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                           <link>
|                             about="#mwt251"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                             href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                             rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                         <div>
|                           about="#mwt250"
|                           class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                           id="mwAfU"
|                           role="note"
|                           "Main article: "
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XHTML"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="XHTML"
|                             "XHTML"
|                         "
"
|                         <p>
|                           id="mwAfY"
|                           "XHTML is a separate language that began as a reformulation of HTML 4.01 using "
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML"
|                             id="mwAfc"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="XML"
|                             "XML"
|                           " 1.0. It is now referred to as "
|                           <i>
|                             id="mwAfg"
|                             "the XML syntax for HTML"
|                           " and is no longer being developed as a separate standard."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt254"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-60"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-60"
|                               id="mwAfk"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwAfo"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAfs"
|                                   "["
|                                 "59"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwAfw"
|                                   "]"
|                         "
"
|                         <ul>
|                           id="mwAf0"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwAf4"
|                             "XHTML 1.0 was published as a W3C Recommendation on January 26, 2000,"
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt257"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-61"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-61"
|                                 id="mwAf8"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAgA"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgE"
|                                     "["
|                                   "60"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgI"
|                                     "]"
|                             " and was later revised and republished on August 1, 2002. It offers the same three variations as HTML 4.0 and 4.01, reformulated in XML, with minor restrictions."
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwAgM"
|                             "XHTML 1.1"
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt260"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-62"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-62"
|                                 id="mwAgQ"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAgU"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgY"
|                                     "["
|                                   "61"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgc"
|                                     "]"
|                             " was published as a W3C Recommendation on May 31, 2001. It is based on XHTML 1.0 Strict, but includes minor changes, can be customized, and is reformulated using modules in the W3C recommendation "Modularization of XHTML", which was published on April 10, 2001."
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt263"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-63"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-63"
|                                 id="mwAgg"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAgk"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgo"
|                                     "["
|                                   "62"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAgs"
|                                     "]"
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwAgw"
|                             "XHTML 2.0 was a working draft. Work on it was abandoned in 2009 in favor of work on "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML5"
|                               id="mwAg0"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="HTML5"
|                               "HTML5"
|                             " and "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XHTML#XHTML5"
|                               id="mwAg4"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="XHTML"
|                               "XHTML5"
|                             "."
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt266"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-64"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-64"
|                                 id="mwAg8"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAhA"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAhE"
|                                     "["
|                                   "63"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAhI"
|                                     "]"
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt269"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-65"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-65"
|                                 id="mwAhM"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAhQ"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAhU"
|                                     "["
|                                   "64"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAhY"
|                                     "]"
|                             <sup>
|                               about="#mwt272"
|                               class="mw-ref reference"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66"}}"
|                               id="cite_ref-66"
|                               rel="dc:references"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                               <a>
|                                 href="#cite_note-66"
|                                 id="mwAhc"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                   id="mwAhg"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAhk"
|                                     "["
|                                   "65"
|                                   <span>
|                                     class="cite-bracket"
|                                     id="mwAho"
|                                     "]"
|                             " XHTML 2.0 was incompatible with XHTML 1.x and, therefore, would be more accurately characterized as an XHTML-inspired new language than an update to XHTML 1.x."
|                         "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Transition_of_HTML_publication_to_WHATWG"
|                       data-mw-section-id="10"
|                       id="mwAhs"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Transition_of_HTML_publication_to_WHATWG"
|                           "Transition of HTML publication to WHATWG"
|                       "
"
|                       <span>
|                         about="#mwt273"
|                         class="mw-empty-elt"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"HTML5#W3C and WHATWG conflict"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwAhw"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt274"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                           href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                           rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt273"
|                         class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                         id="mwAh0"
|                         role="note"
|                         "See also: "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML5#W3C_and_WHATWG_conflict"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTML5"
|                           "HTML5 §"
|                           <span>
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             " "
|                           "W3C and WHATWG conflict"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwAh4"
|                         "On 28 May 2019, the W3C announced that WHATWG would be the sole publisher of the HTML and DOM standards."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt277"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"W3C transfer blog"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-W3C_transfer_blog-67"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-W3C_transfer_blog_67-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-W3C_transfer_blog-67"
|                             id="mwAh8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwAiA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAiE"
|                                 "["
|                               "66"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAiI"
|                                 "]"
|                         <sup>
