|                                 "]"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt286"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"W3C transfer ZDNet"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-W3C_transfer_ZDNet-70"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-W3C_transfer_ZDNet_70-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-W3C_transfer_ZDNet-70"
|                             id="mwAis"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwAiw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAi0"
|                                 "["
|                               "69"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAi4"
|                                 "]"
|                         " The W3C and WHATWG had been publishing competing standards since 2012. While the W3C standard was identical to the WHATWG in 2007 the standards have since progressively diverged due to different design decisions."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt289"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"W3C forks"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-W3C_forks-71"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-W3C_forks_71-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-W3C_forks-71"
|                             id="mwAi8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwAjA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAjE"
|                                 "["
|                               "70"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAjI"
|                                 "]"
|                         " The WHATWG "Living Standard" had been the "
|                         <i>
|                           id="mwAjM"
|                           "de facto"
|                         " web standard for some time."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt292"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-72"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-72"
|                             id="mwAjQ"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwAjU"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAjY"
|                                 "["
|                               "71"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwAjc"
|                                 "]"
|                         " The W3C periodically reviews and publishes snapshots of the WHATWG HTML specification as W3C Recommendations."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt295"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-73"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-73"
