|                                       id="mwBBE"
|                                       "em"
|                                     <span>
|                                       class="p"
|                                       id="mwBBI"
|                                       ">"
|                                   " respectively. It is easier to see how an aural user agent should interpret the latter two elements. However, they are not equivalent to their presentational counterparts: it would be undesirable for a screen reader to emphasize the name of a book, for instance, but on a screen, such a name would be italicized. Most presentational markup elements have become "
|                                   <a>
|                                     href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deprecation"
|                                     id="mwBBM"
|                                     rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                                     title="Deprecation"
|                                     "deprecated"
|                                   " under the HTML 4.0 specification in favor of using "
|                                   <a>
|                                     href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS"
|                                     id="mwBBQ"
|                                     rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                                     title="CSS"
|                                     "CSS"
|                                   " for styling."
|                             "
"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBBU"
|                               "Hypertext markup makes parts of a document into links to other documents: 
"
|                               <ul>
|                                 id="mwBBY"
|                                 <li>
|                                   id="mwBBc"
|                                   "An anchor element creates a "
|                                   <a>
|                                     href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperlink"
|                                     id="mwBBg"
|                                     rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                                     title="Hyperlink"
|                                     "hyperlink"
|                                   " in the document and its "
|                                   <code>
|                                     id="mwBBk"
|                                     "href"
|                                   " attribute sets the link's target "
|                                   <a>
|                                     href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/URL"
|                                     id="mwBBo"
|                                     rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                                     title="URL"
|                                     "URL"
|                                   ". For example, the HTML markup "
|                                   <code>
|                                     about="#mwt395"
|                                     class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                                     data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/\">Wikipedia</a>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/\">Wikipedia</a>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                                     dir="ltr"
