|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-78"
|                               id="mwBFA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwBFE"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFI"
|                                   "["
|                                 "77"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFM"
|                                   "]"
|                           " Leaving attribute values unquoted is considered unsafe."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt409"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-79"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-79"
|                               id="mwBFQ"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwBFU"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFY"
|                                   "["
|                                 "78"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFc"
|                                   "]"
|                           " In contrast with name-value pair attributes, there are some attributes that affect the element simply by their presence in the start tag of the element,"
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt412"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"tagshtml"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-tagshtml-8"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-tagshtml_8-2"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-tagshtml-8"
|                               id="mwBFg"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwBFk"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFo"
|                                   "["
|                                 "7"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBFs"
|                                   "]"
|                           " like the "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBFw"
|                             "ismap"
|                           " attribute for the "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBF0"
|                             "img"
|                           " element."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt415"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-80"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-80"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-80"
|                               id="mwBF4"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwBF8"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBGA"
|                                   "["
|                                 "79"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBGE"
|                                   "]"
|                         "

"
|                         <p>
|                           id="mwBGI"
|                           "There are several common attributes that may appear in many elements:"
|                         "
"
|                         <ul>
|                           id="mwBGM"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwBGQ"
|                             "The "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBGU"
|                               "id"
|                             " attribute provides a document-wide unique identifier for an element. This is used to identify the element so that stylesheets can alter its presentational properties, and scripts may alter, animate or delete its contents or presentation. Appended to the URL of the page, it provides a globally unique identifier for the element, typically a sub-section of the page. For example, the ID "Attributes" in "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBGY"
|                               <span>
|                                 id="mwBGc"
|                                 typeof="mw:Nowiki"
|                                 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML#Attributes"
|                             "."
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwBGg"
|                             "The "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBGk"
|                               "class"
|                             " attribute provides a way of classifying similar elements. This can be used for "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantics"
|                               id="mwBGo"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Semantics"
|                               "semantic"
|                             " or presentation purposes. For example, an HTML document might semantically use the designation "
|                             <code>
|                               about="#mwt416"
|                               class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<class=\"notation\">"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<class=\"notation\">"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                               dir="ltr"
|                               id="mwBGs"
|                               style=""
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="p"
|                                 id="mwBGw"
|                                 "<"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="nt"
|                                 id="mwBG0"
|                                 "class"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="err"
|                                 id="mwBG4"
|                                 "=""
|                               <span>
|                                 class="na"
|                                 id="mwBG8"
|                                 "notation"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="err"
|                                 id="mwBHA"
|                                 """
|                               <span>
|                                 class="p"
|                                 id="mwBHE"
|                                 ">"
|                             " to indicate that all elements with this class value are subordinate to the main text of the document. In presentation"
|                             <!--  Presentationally is not a formally accepted word  -->
|                             ", such elements might be gathered together and presented as footnotes on a page instead of appearing in the place where they occur in the HTML source. Class attributes are used semantically in "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microformat"
|                               id="mwBHI"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Microformat"
|                               "microformats"
|                             ". Multiple class values may be specified; for example "
|                             <code>
|                               about="#mwt418"
|                               class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<class=\"notation important\">"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<class=\"notation important\">"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                               dir="ltr"
|                               id="mwBHM"
|                               style=""
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="p"
|                                 id="mwBHQ"
|                                 "<"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="nt"
|                                 id="mwBHU"
|                                 "class"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="err"
|                                 id="mwBHY"
|                                 "=""
|                               <span>
|                                 class="na"
|                                 id="mwBHc"
|                                 "notation"
|                               " "
|                               <span>
|                                 class="na"
|                                 id="mwBHg"
|                                 "important"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="err"
|                                 id="mwBHk"
|                                 """
|                               <span>
|                                 class="p"
|                                 id="mwBHo"
|                                 ">"
|                             " puts the element into both the "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBHs"
|                               "notation"
|                             " and the "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBHw"
|                               "important"
|                             " classes."
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwBH0"
|                             "An author may use the "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBH4"
|                               "style"
|                             " attribute to assign presentational properties to a particular element. It is considered better practice to use an element's "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBH8"
|                               "id"
|                             " or "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBIA"
|                               "class"
|                             " attributes to select the element from within a "
|                             <a>
|                               class="mw-redirect"
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascading_Style_Sheets"
|                               id="mwBIE"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Cascading Style Sheets"
|                               "stylesheet"
|                             ", though sometimes this can be too cumbersome for a simple, specific, or ad hoc styling."
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwBII"
|                             "The "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBIM"
|                               "title"
|                             " attribute is used to attach a subtextual explanation to an element. In most "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser"
|                               id="mwBIQ"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Web browser"
|                               "browsers"
|                             " this attribute is displayed as a "
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tooltip"
|                               id="mwBIU"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Tooltip"
|                               "tooltip"
|                             "."
|                           "
"
|                           <li>
|                             id="mwBIY"
|                             "The "
|                             <code>
|                               id="mwBIc"
|                               "lang"
|                             " attribute identifies the natural language of the element's contents, which may be different from that of the rest of the document. For example, in an English-language document: "
|                             <div>
|                               about="#mwt420"
|                               class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                               data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html"},"body":{"extsrc":"<p>Oh well, <span lang=\"fr\">c'est la vie</span>, as they say in France.</p>"}}"
|                               dir="ltr"
|                               id="mwBIg"
|                               typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight"
|                               <pre>
|                                 id="mwBIk"
|                                 <span>
|                                   id="mwBIo"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBIs"
|                                   "<"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="nt"
|                                   id="mwBIw"
|                                   "p"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBI0"
|                                   ">"
|                                 "Oh well, "
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBI4"
|                                   "<"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="nt"
|                                   id="mwBI8"
|                                   "span"
|                                 " "
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="na"
|                                   id="mwBJA"
|                                   "lang"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="o"
|                                   id="mwBJE"
|                                   "="
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="s"
|                                   id="mwBJI"
|                                   ""fr""
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBJM"
|                                   ">"
|                                 "c'est la vie"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBJQ"
|                                   "</"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="nt"
|                                   id="mwBJU"
|                                   "span"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBJY"
|                                   ">"
|                                 ", as they say in France."
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBJc"
|                                   "</"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="nt"
|                                   id="mwBJg"
|                                   "p"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="p"
|                                   id="mwBJk"
|                                   ">"
|                                 "
"
|                         "

"
|                         <p>
|                           id="mwBJo"
|                           "The abbreviation element, "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBJs"
|                             "abbr"
|                           ", can be used to demonstrate some of these attributes:"
|                         "

"
|                         <div>
|                           about="#mwt421"
|                           class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html"},"body":{"extsrc":"<abbr id=\"anId\" class=\"jargon\" style=\"color:purple;\" title=\"Hypertext Markup Language\">HTML</abbr>"}}"
|                           dir="ltr"
|                           id="mwBJw"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight"
|                           <pre>
|                             id="mwBJ0"
|                             <span>
|                               id="mwBJ4"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBJ8"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBKA"
|                               "abbr"
|                             " "
|                             <span>
|                               class="na"
|                               id="mwBKE"
|                               "id"
|                             <span>
|                               class="o"
|                               id="mwBKI"
|                               "="
|                             <span>
|                               class="s"
|                               id="mwBKM"
|                               ""anId""
|                             " "
|                             <span>
|                               class="na"
|                               id="mwBKQ"
|                               "class"
|                             <span>
|                               class="o"
|                               id="mwBKU"
|                               "="
|                             <span>
|                               class="s"
|                               id="mwBKY"
|                               ""jargon""
|                             " "
|                             <span>
|                               class="na"
|                               id="mwBKc"
|                               "style"
|                             <span>
|                               class="o"
|                               id="mwBKg"
|                               "="
|                             <span>
|                               class="s"
|                               id="mwBKk"
|                               ""color:purple;""
|                             " "
|                             <span>
|                               class="na"
|                               id="mwBKo"
|                               "title"
|                             <span>
|                               class="o"
|                               id="mwBKs"
|                               "="
|                             <span>
|                               class="s"
|                               id="mwBKw"
|                               ""Hypertext Markup Language""
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBK0"
|                               ">"
|                             "HTML"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBK4"
|                               "</"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBK8"
|                               "abbr"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBLA"
|                               ">"
|                             "
"
|                         "

"
|                         <p>
|                           id="mwBLE"
|                           "This example displays as "
|                           <abbr>
|                             class="jargon"
|                             id="anId"
|                             style="color:purple;"
|                             title="Hypertext Markup Language"
|                             "HTML"
|                           "; in most browsers, pointing the cursor at the abbreviation should display the title text "Hypertext Markup Language.""
|                         "

"
|                         <p>
|                           id="mwBLI"
|                           "Most elements take the language-related attribute "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBLM"
|                             "dir"
|                           " to specify text direction, such as with "rtl" for right-to-left text in, for example, "
|                           <a>
|                             class="mw-redirect"
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arabic_language"
|                             id="mwBLQ"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Arabic language"
|                             "Arabic"
|                           ", "
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_language"
|                             id="mwBLU"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Persian language"
|                             "Persian"
|                           " or "
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebrew_language"
|                             id="mwBLY"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Hebrew language"
|                             "Hebrew"
|                           "."
|                           <sup>
|                             about="#mwt424"
|                             class="mw-ref reference"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-81"}}"
|                             id="cite_ref-81"
|                             rel="dc:references"
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                             <a>
|                               href="#cite_note-81"
|                               id="mwBLc"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="mw-reflink-text"
|                                 id="mwBLg"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBLk"
|                                   "["
|                                 "80"
|                                 <span>
|                                   class="cite-bracket"
|                                   id="mwBLo"
|                                   "]"
|                         "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Character_and_entity_references"
|                       data-mw-section-id="20"
|                       id="mwBLs"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Character_and_entity_references"
|                           "Character and entity references"
|                       "
"
|                       <span>
|                         about="#mwt425"
|                         class="mw-empty-elt"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"List of XML and HTML character entity references"},"2":{"wt":"Unicode and HTML"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBLw"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt426"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                           href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                           rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt425"
|                         class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                         id="mwBL0"
|                         role="note"
|                         "See also: "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_XML_and_HTML_character_entity_references"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="List of XML and HTML character entity references"
|                           "List of XML and HTML character entity references"
|                         " and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode_and_HTML"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Unicode and HTML"
|                           "Unicode and HTML"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBL4"
|                         "As of version 4.0, HTML defines a set of 252 "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_entity_reference"
|                           id="mwBL8"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Character entity reference"
|                           "character entity references"
|                         " and a set of 1,114,050 "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Numeric_character_reference"
|                           id="mwBMA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Numeric character reference"
|                           "numeric character references"
|                         ", both of which allow individual characters to be written via simple markup, rather than literally. A literal character and its markup counterpart are considered equivalent and are rendered identically."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBME"
|                         "The ability to ""
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escape_character"
|                           id="mwBMI"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Escape character"
|                           "escape"
|                         "" characters in this way allows for the characters "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBMM"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBMQ"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "<"
|                         " and "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBMU"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBMY"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                         " (when written as "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBMc"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBMg"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "lt;"
|                         " and "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBMk"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBMo"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "amp;"
|                         ", respectively) to be interpreted as character data, rather than markup. For example, a literal "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBMs"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBMw"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "<"
|                         " normally indicates the start of a tag, and "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBM0"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBM4"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                         " normally indicates the start of a character entity reference or numeric character reference; writing it as "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBM8"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNA"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "amp;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNE"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNI"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#x26;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNM"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNQ"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#38;"
|                         " allows "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNU"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNY"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                         " to be included in the content of an element or in the value of an attribute. The double-quote character ("
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNc"
|                           """
|                         "), when not used to quote an attribute value, must also be escaped as "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNg"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNk"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "quot;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNo"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBNs"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#x22;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBNw"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBN0"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#34;"
|                         " when it appears within the attribute value itself. Equivalently, the single-quote character ("
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBN4"
|                           "'"
|                         "), when not used to quote an attribute value, must also be escaped as "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBN8"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBOA"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#x27;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBOE"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBOI"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#39;"
|                         " (or as "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBOM"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBOQ"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "apos;"
|                         " in HTML5 or XHTML documents"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt429"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-82"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-82"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-82"
|                             id="mwBOU"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBOY"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBOc"
|                                 "["
|                               "81"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBOg"
|                                 "]"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt432"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"aposhtml"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-aposhtml-83"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-aposhtml_83-0"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-aposhtml-83"
|                             id="mwBOk"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBOo"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBOs"
|                                 "["
|                               "82"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBOw"
|                                 "]"
|                         ") when it appears within the attribute value itself. If document authors overlook the need to escape such characters, some browsers can be very forgiving and try to use context to guess their intent. The result is still invalid markup, which makes the document less accessible to other browsers and to other "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_agent"
|                           id="mwBO0"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="User agent"
|                           "user agents"
|                         " that may try to parse the document for "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_crawler"
|                           id="mwBO4"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Web crawler"
|                           "search and indexing"
|                         " purposes for example."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBO8"
|                         "Escaping also allows for characters that are not easily typed, or that are not available in the document's "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_encoding"
|                           id="mwBPA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Character encoding"
|                           "character encoding"
|                         ", to be represented within the element and attribute content. For example, the acute-accented "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBPE"
|                           "e"
|                         " ("
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBPI"
|                           "é"
|                         "), a character typically found only on Western European and South American keyboards, can be written in any HTML document as the entity reference "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBPM"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBPQ"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "eacute;"
|                         " or as the numeric references "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBPU"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBPY"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#xE9;"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBPc"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBPg"
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "&"
|                           "#233;"
|                         ", using characters that are available on all keyboards and are supported in all character encodings. "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode"
|                           id="mwBPk"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Unicode"
|                           "Unicode"
|                         " character encodings such as "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UTF-8"
|                           id="mwBPo"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="UTF-8"
|                           "UTF-8"
|                         " are compatible with all modern browsers and allow direct access to almost all the characters of the world's writing systems."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt435"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-84"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
