"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Data_types"
|                       data-mw-section-id="21"
|                       id="mwBY4"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Data_types"
|                           "Data types"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBY8"
|                         "HTML defines several "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_type"
|                           id="mwBZA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Data type"
|                           "data types"
|                         " for element content, such as script data and stylesheet data, and a plethora of types for attribute values, including IDs, names, "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_Resource_Identifier"
|                           id="mwBZE"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Uniform Resource Identifier"
|                           "URIs"
|                         ", numbers, units of length, languages, media descriptors, colors, character encodings, dates and times, and so on. All of these data types are specializations of character data."
|                       "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Document_type_declaration"
|                       data-mw-section-id="22"
|                       id="mwBZI"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Document_type_declaration"
|                           "Document type declaration"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBZM"
|                         "HTML documents are required to start with a "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Document_type_declaration"
|                           id="mwBZQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Document type declaration"
|                           "document type declaration"
|                         " (informally, a "doctype"). In browsers, the doctype helps to define the rendering mode—particularly whether to use "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quirks_mode"
|                           id="mwBZU"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Quirks mode"
|                           "quirks mode"
|                         "."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBZY"
|                         "The original purpose of the doctype was to enable the parsing and validation of HTML documents by SGML tools based on the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Document_type_definition"
|                           id="mwBZc"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Document type definition"
|                           "document type definition"
|                         " (DTD). The DTD to which the DOCTYPE refers contains a machine-readable grammar specifying the permitted and prohibited content for a document conforming to such a DTD. Browsers, on the other hand, do not implement HTML as an application of SGML and as consequence do not read the DTD."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBZg"
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML5"
|                           id="mwBZk"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTML5"
|                           "HTML5"
|                         " does not define a DTD; therefore, in HTML5 the doctype declaration is simpler and shorter:"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt524"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-85"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-85"
|                             id="mwBZo"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBZs"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBZw"
|                                 "["
|                               "84"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBZ0"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt525"
|                         class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-dtd mw-content-ltr"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"dtd"},"body":{"extsrc":"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n"}}"
|                         dir="ltr"
|                         id="mwBZ4"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight"
|                         <pre>
|                           id="mwBZ8"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBaA"
|                           <span>
|                             class="k"
|                             id="mwBaE"
|                             "<!DOCTYPE"
|                           " "
|                           <span>
|                             class="nt"
|                             id="mwBaI"
|                             "html"
|                           <span>
|                             class="k"
|                             id="mwBaM"
|                             ">"
|                           "
"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBaQ"
|                         "An example of an HTML 4 doctype"
|                       "

"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt526"
|                         class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-dtd mw-content-ltr"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"dtd"},"body":{"extsrc":"\n<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"https://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd\">\n"}}"
|                         dir="ltr"
|                         id="mwBaU"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight"
|                         <pre>
|                           id="mwBaY"
|                           <span>
|                             id="mwBac"
|                           <span>
|                             class="k"
|                             id="mwBag"
|                             "<!DOCTYPE"
|                           " "
|                           <span>
|                             class="nt"
|                             id="mwBak"
|                             "HTML"
|                           " "
|                           <span>
|                             class="kc"
|                             id="mwBao"
|                             "PUBLIC"
|                           " "
|                           <span>
|                             class="s2"
|                             id="mwBas"
|                             ""-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN""
|                           " "
|                           <span>
|                             class="s2"
|                             id="mwBaw"
|                             ""https://www.w3.org/TR/html4/strict.dtd""
|                           <span>
|                             class="k"
|                             id="mwBa0"
|                             ">"
|                           "
"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBa4"
|                         "This declaration references the DTD for the "strict" version of HTML 4.01. SGML-based validators read the DTD in order to properly parse the document and to perform validation. In modern browsers, a valid doctype activates standards mode as opposed to "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quirks_mode"
|                           id="mwBa8"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Quirks mode"
|                           "quirks mode"
|                         "."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBbA"
|                         "In addition, HTML 4.01 provides Transitional and Frameset DTDs, "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-selflink-fragment"
|                           href="#Transitional_versus_strict"
|                           id="mwBbE"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           "as explained below"
|                         ". The transitional type is the most inclusive, incorporating current tags as well as older or "deprecated" tags, with the Strict DTD excluding deprecated tags. The frameset has all tags necessary to make frames on a page along with the tags included in transitional type."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt529"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-86"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-86"
|                             id="mwBbI"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBbM"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBbQ"
|                                 "["
|                               "85"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBbU"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                   <section>
|                     aria-labelledby="Semantic_HTML"
|                     data-mw-section-id="23"
|                     id="mwBbY"
|                     <div>
|                       class="mw-heading mw-heading2"
|                       <h2>
|                         id="Semantic_HTML"
|                         "Semantic HTML"
|                     "
"
|                     <span>
|                       about="#mwt530"
|                       class="mw-empty-elt"
|                       data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Semantic HTML"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                       id="mwBbc"
|                       typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                       <link>
|                         about="#mwt531"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                         href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                         rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                     <div>
|                       about="#mwt530"
|                       class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                       id="mwBbg"
|                       role="note"
|                       "Main article: "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_HTML"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Semantic HTML"
|                         "Semantic HTML"
|                     "
"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBbk"
|                       "Semantic HTML is a way of writing HTML that emphasizes the meaning of the encoded information over its presentation (look). HTML has included semantic markup from its inception,"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt537"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-87"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-87"
|                           id="mwBbo"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBbs"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBbw"
|                               "["
|                             "86"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBb0"
|                               "]"
|                       " but has also included presentational markup, such as "
|                       <code>
|                         about="#mwt532"
|                         class="nowrap"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"tag","href":"./Template:Tag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"font"},"2":{"wt":"open"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBb4"
|                         style=""
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "<"
|                         "font"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           ">"
|                       ", "
|                       <code>
|                         about="#mwt533"
|                         class="nowrap"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"tag","href":"./Template:Tag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"i"},"2":{"wt":"open"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBb8"
|                         style=""
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "<"
|                         "i"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           ">"
|                       ", and "
|                       <code>
|                         about="#mwt534"
|                         class="nowrap"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"tag","href":"./Template:Tag"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"center"},"2":{"wt":"open"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBcA"
|                         style=""
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "<"
|                         "center"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           ">"
|                       " tags. There are also the semantically neutral "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Div_and_span"
|                         id="mwBcE"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Div and span"
|                         "div and span"
|                       " tags. Since the late 1990s, when "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascading_Style_Sheets"
|                         id="mwBcI"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Cascading Style Sheets"
|                         "Cascading Style Sheets"
|                       " were beginning to work in most browsers, web authors have been encouraged to avoid the use of presentational HTML markup with a view to the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Separation_of_content_and_presentation"
|                         id="mwBcM"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Separation of content and presentation"
|                         "separation of content and presentation"
|                       "."
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt540"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-88"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-88"
|                           id="mwBcQ"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBcU"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBcY"
|                               "["
|                             "87"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBcc"
|                               "]"
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBcg"
|                       "In a 2001 discussion of the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_Web"
|                         id="mwBck"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Semantic Web"
|                         "Semantic Web"
|                       ", "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tim_Berners-Lee"
|                         id="mwBco"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Tim Berners-Lee"
|                         "Tim Berners-Lee"
|                       " and others gave examples of ways in which intelligent software "agents" may one day automatically crawl the web and find, filter, and correlate previously unrelated, published facts for the benefit of human users."
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt545"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-89"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-89"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-89"
|                           id="mwBcs"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBcw"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBc0"
|                               "["
|                             "88"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBc4"
|                               "]"
|                       " Such agents are not commonplace even now"
|                       <link>
|                         about="#mwt541"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"when","href":"./Template:When"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2026"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         href="./Category:All_articles_with_vague_or_ambiguous_time"
|                         id="mwBc8"
|                         rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                       <link>
|                         about="#mwt541"
|                         href="./Category:Vague_or_ambiguous_time_from_February_2026"
|                         rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt541"
|                         class="noprint Inline-Template "
|                         id="mwBdA"
|                         style="white-space:nowrap;"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "["
|                         <i>
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Dates_and_numbers#Chronological_items"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Wikipedia:Manual of Style/Dates and numbers"
|                             <span>
|                               title="The time period mentioned near this tag is ambiguous. (February 2026)"
|                               "when?"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "]"
|                       ", but some of the ideas of "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_2.0"
|                         id="mwBdE"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web 2.0"
|                         "Web 2.0"
|                       ", "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashup_(web_application_hybrid)"
|                         id="mwBdI"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Mashup (web application hybrid)"
|                         "mashups"
|                       " and "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Price_comparison_service"
|                         id="mwBdM"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Price comparison service"
|                         "price comparison websites"
|                       " may be coming close"
|                       <link>
|                         about="#mwt542"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"citation needed","href":"./Template:Citation_needed"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 2025"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements"
|                         id="mwBdQ"
|                         rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                       <link>
|                         about="#mwt542"
|                         href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_February_2025"
|                         rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt542"
|                         class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact"
|                         id="mwBdU"
|                         style="white-space:nowrap;"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "["
|                         <i>
|                           <a>
|                             href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed"
|                             rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                             title="Wikipedia:Citation needed"
|                             <span>
|                               title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (February 2025)"
|                               "citation needed"
|                         <span>
|                           typeof="mw:Entity"
|                           "]"
|                       ". The main difference between these web application hybrids and Berners-Lee's semantic agents lies in the fact that the current "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feed_aggregator"
|                         id="mwBdY"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Feed aggregator"
|                         "aggregation"
|                       " and hybridization of information is usually designed by "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_developer"
|                         id="mwBdc"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web developer"
|                         "web developers"
|                       ", who already know the web locations and the "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_programming_interface"
|                         id="mwBdg"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Application programming interface"
|                         "API semantics"
|                       " of the specific data they wish to mash, compare and combine."
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBdk"
|                       "An important type of web agent that does crawl and read web pages automatically, without prior knowledge of what it might find, is the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_crawler"
|                         id="mwBdo"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web crawler"
|                         "web crawler"
|                       " or search-engine spider. These software agents are dependent on the semantic clarity of web pages they find as they use various techniques and "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithm"
|                         id="mwBds"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Algorithm"
|                         "algorithms"
|                       " to read and index millions of web pages a day and provide web users with "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_search_engine"
|                         id="mwBdw"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web search engine"
|                         "search facilities"
|                       " without which the World Wide Web's usefulness would be greatly reduced."
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBd0"
|                       "In order for search engine spiders to be able to rate the significance of pieces of text they find in HTML documents, and also for those creating mashups and other hybrids as well as for more automated agents as they are developed, the semantic structures that exist in HTML need to be widely and uniformly applied to bring out the meaning of the published text."
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt548"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Semantic_Web_Revisted"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Semantic_Web_Revisted-90"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-Semantic_Web_Revisted_90-0"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-Semantic_Web_Revisted-90"
|                           id="mwBd4"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBd8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBeA"
|                               "["
|                             "89"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBeE"
|                               "]"
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBeI"
|                       "Presentational markup tags are "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deprecation"
|                         id="mwBeM"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Deprecation"
|                         "deprecated"
|                       " in current HTML and "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XHTML"
|                         id="mwBeQ"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="XHTML"
|                         "XHTML"
|                       " recommendations. The majority of presentational features from previous versions of HTML are no longer allowed as they lead to poorer accessibility, higher cost of site maintenance, and larger document sizes."
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt551"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-91"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-91"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-91"
|                           id="mwBeU"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBeY"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBec"
|                               "["
|                             "90"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBeg"
|                               "]"
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBek"
|                       "Good semantic HTML also improves the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accessibility"
|                         id="mwBeo"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Accessibility"
|                         "accessibility"
|                       " of web documents (see also "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_Content_Accessibility_Guidelines"
|                         id="mwBes"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web Content Accessibility Guidelines"
|                         "Web Content Accessibility Guidelines"
|                       "). For example, when a screen reader or audio browser can correctly ascertain the structure of a document, it will not waste the visually impaired user's time by reading out repeated or irrelevant information when it has been marked up correctly."
|                     "

"
|                   <section>
|                     aria-labelledby="Delivery"
|                     data-mw-section-id="24"
|                     id="mwBew"
|                     <div>
|                       class="mw-heading mw-heading2"
|                       <h2>
|                         id="Delivery"
|                         "Delivery"
|                     "
"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBe0"
|                       "HTML documents can be delivered by the same means as any other computer file. However, they are most often delivered either by "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP"
|                         id="mwBe4"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="HTTP"
|                         "HTTP"
|                       " from a "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_server"
|                         id="mwBe8"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Web server"
|                         "web server"
|                       " or by "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email"
|                         id="mwBfA"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Email"
|                         "email"
|                       "."
|                     "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="HTTP"
|                       data-mw-section-id="25"
|                       id="mwBfE"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="HTTP"
|                           "HTTP"
|                       "
"
|                       <span>
|                         about="#mwt552"
|                         class="mw-empty-elt"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"HTTP"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBfI"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt553"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                           href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                           rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt552"
|                         class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                         id="mwBfM"
|                         role="note"
|                         "Main article: "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTTP"
|                           "HTTP"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBfQ"
|                         "The "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Web"
|                           id="mwBfU"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="World Wide Web"
|                           "World Wide Web"
|                         " is composed primarily of HTML documents transmitted from web servers to web browsers using the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP"
|                           id="mwBfY"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTTP"
|                           "Hypertext Transfer Protocol"
|                         " (HTTP). However, HTTP is used to serve images, sound, and other content, in addition to HTML. To allow the web browser to know how to handle each document it receives, other information is transmitted along with the document. This "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_data"
|                           id="mwBfc"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Meta data"
|                           "meta data"
|                         " usually includes the "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIME_type"
|                           id="mwBfg"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="MIME type"
|                           "MIME type"
|                         " (e.g., "
|                         <kbd>
|                           id="mwBfk"
|                           "text/html"
|                         " or "
|                         <kbd>
|                           id="mwBfo"
|                           "application/xhtml+xml"
|                         ") and the character encoding (see "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_encodings_in_HTML"
|                           id="mwBfs"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Character encodings in HTML"
|                           "Character encodings in HTML"
|                         ")."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBfw"
|                         "In modern browsers, the MIME type that is sent with the HTML document may affect how the document is initially interpreted. A document sent with the XHTML MIME type is expected to be "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Well-formed_document"
|                           id="mwBf0"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Well-formed document"
|                           "well-formed"
|                         " XML; syntax errors may cause the browser to fail to render it. The same document sent with the HTML MIME type might be displayed successfully since some browsers are more lenient with HTML."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBf4"
|                         "The W3C recommendations state that XHTML 1.0 documents that follow guidelines set forth in the recommendation's Appendix C may be labeled with either MIME Type."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt565"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-92"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-92"
|                             id="mwBf8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBgA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgE"
|                                 "["
|                               "91"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgI"
|                                 "]"
|                         " XHTML 1.1 also states that XHTML 1.1 documents should"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt554"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":""},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Ref RFC","href":"./Template:Ref_RFC"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2119"},"quote":{"wt":"3. SHOULD This word, or the adjective \"RECOMMENDED\", mean that there may exist valid reasons in particular circumstances to ignore a particular item, but the full implications must be understood and carefully weighed before choosing a different course."}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           id="cite_ref-93"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-93"
|                             id="mwBgM"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBgQ"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgU"
|                                 "["
|                               "92"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgY"
|                                 "]"
|                         " be labeled with either MIME type."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt568"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-94"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-94"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-94"
|                             id="mwBgc"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBgg"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgk"
|                                 "["
|                               "93"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBgo"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="HTML_e-mail"
|                       data-mw-section-id="26"
|                       id="mwBgs"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="HTML_e-mail"
|                           "HTML e-mail"
|                       "
"
|                       <span>
|                         about="#mwt569"
|                         class="mw-empty-elt"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"HTML email"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBgw"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt570"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                           href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                           rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt569"
|                         class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                         id="mwBg0"
|                         role="note"
|                         "Main article: "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML_email"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTML email"
|                           "HTML email"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBg4"
|                         "Most graphical email clients allow the use of a subset of HTML (often ill-defined) to provide formatting and "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_web"
|                           id="mwBg8"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Semantic web"
|                           "semantic"
|                         " markup not available with "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_text"
|                           id="mwBhA"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Plain text"
|                           "plain text"
|                         ". This may include typographic information like colored headings, emphasized and quoted text, inline images and diagrams. Many such clients include both a "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphical_user_interface"
|                           id="mwBhE"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Graphical user interface"
|                           "GUI"
|                         " editor for composing HTML e-mail messages and a rendering engine for displaying them. Use of HTML in e-mail is criticized by some because of compatibility issues, because it can help disguise "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phishing"
|                           id="mwBhI"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Phishing"
|                           "phishing"
|                         " attacks, because of accessibility issues for blind or visually impaired people, because it can confuse "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Email_spam"
|                           id="mwBhM"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Email spam"
|                           "spam"
|                         " filters and because the message size is larger than plain text."
|                       "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Naming_conventions"
|                       data-mw-section-id="27"
|                       id="mwBhQ"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Naming_conventions"
|                           "Naming conventions"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBhU"
|                         "The most common "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filename_extension"
|                           id="mwBhY"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Filename extension"
|                           "filename extension"
|                         " for "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_file"
|                           id="mwBhc"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Computer file"
|                           "files"
|                         " containing HTML is "
|                         <kbd>
|                           id="mwBhg"
|                           ".html"
|                         ". A common abbreviation of this is "
|                         <kbd>
|                           id="mwBhk"
|                           ".htm"
|                         ", which originated because some operating systems limit file extensions to "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8.3_filename"
|                           id="mwBho"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="8.3 filename"
|                           "three letters"
|                         "."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt573"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-95"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-95"
|                             id="mwBhs"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBhw"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBh0"
|                                 "["
|                               "94"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBh4"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="HTML_Application"
|                       data-mw-section-id="28"
|                       id="mwBh8"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="HTML_Application"
|                           "HTML Application"
|                       "
"
|                       <span>
|                         about="#mwt574"
|                         class="mw-empty-elt"
|                         data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"HTML Application"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                         id="mwBiA"
|                         typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt575"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}"
|                           href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237"
|                           rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles"
|                       <div>
|                         about="#mwt574"
|                         class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable"
|                         id="mwBiE"
|                         role="note"
|                         "Main article: "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML_Application"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTML Application"
|                           "HTML Application"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBiI"
|                         "An HTML Application (HTA; file extension "
|                         <kbd>
|                           id="mwBiM"
|                           ".hta"
|                         ") is a "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Windows"
|                           id="mwBiQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Microsoft Windows"
|                           "Microsoft Windows"
|                         " application that uses HTML and Dynamic HTML in a "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser"
|                           id="mwBiU"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Web browser"
|                           "browser"
|                         " to provide the application's graphical interface. A regular HTML file is confined to the security model of the "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_security"
|                           id="mwBiY"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Browser security"
|                           "web browser's security"
|                         ", communicating only to web servers and manipulating only web page objects and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_cookie"
|                           id="mwBic"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="HTTP cookie"
|                           "site cookies"
|                         ". An HTA runs as a fully trusted application and therefore has more privileges, like creation/editing/removal of files and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Registry"
|                           id="mwBig"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Windows Registry"
|                           "Windows Registry"
|                         " entries. Because they operate outside the browser's security model, HTAs cannot be executed via HTTP, but must be downloaded (just like an "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EXE"
|                           id="mwBik"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="EXE"
|                           "EXE"
|                         " file) and executed from local file system."
|                       "

"
|                   <section>
|                     aria-labelledby="HTML4_variations"
|                     data-mw-section-id="29"
|                     id="mwBio"
|                     <div>
|                       class="mw-heading mw-heading2"
|                       <h2>
|                         id="HTML4_variations"
|                         "HTML4 variations"
|                     "
"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBis"
|                       "Since its inception, HTML and its associated protocols gained acceptance relatively quickly. However, no clear standards existed in the early years of the language. Though its creators originally conceived of HTML as a semantic language devoid of presentation details,"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt577"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-96"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-96"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-96"
|                           id="mwBiw"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBi0"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBi4"
|                               "["
|                             "95"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBi8"
|                               "]"
|                       " practical uses pushed many presentational elements and attributes into the language, driven largely by the various browser vendors. The latest standards surrounding HTML reflect efforts to overcome the sometimes chaotic development of the language"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt579"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-97"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-97"
|                           id="mwBjA"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBjE"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBjI"
|                               "["
|                             "96"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBjM"
|                               "]"
|                       " and to create a rational foundation for building both meaningful and well-presented documents. To return HTML to its role as a semantic language, the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Web_Consortium"
|                         id="mwBjQ"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="World Wide Web Consortium"
|                         "W3C"
|                       " has developed style languages such as "
|                       <a>
|                         class="mw-redirect"
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascading_Style_Sheets"
|                         id="mwBjU"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Cascading Style Sheets"
|                         "CSS"
|                       " and "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XSL"
|                         id="mwBjY"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="XSL"
|                         "XSL"
|                       " to shoulder the burden of presentation. In conjunction, the HTML specification has slowly reined in the presentational elements."
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBjc"
|                       "There are two axes differentiating various variations of HTML as currently specified: SGML-based HTML versus XML-based HTML (referred to as XHTML) on one axis, and strict versus transitional (loose) versus frameset on the other axis."
|                     "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="SGML-based_versus_XML-based_HTML"
|                       data-mw-section-id="30"
|                       id="mwBjg"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="SGML-based_versus_XML-based_HTML"
|                           "SGML-based versus XML-based HTML"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBjk"
|                         "One difference in the latest"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt580"
|                           data-mw="{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"when","href":"./Template:When"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"March 2022"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           href="./Category:All_articles_with_vague_or_ambiguous_time"
|                           id="mwBjo"
|                           rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                           typeof="mw:Transclusion"
|                         <link>
|                           about="#mwt580"
|                           href="./Category:Vague_or_ambiguous_time_from_March_2022"
|                           rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt580"
|                           class="noprint Inline-Template "
|                           id="mwBjs"
|                           style="white-space:nowrap;"
|                           <span>
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "["
|                           <i>
|                             <a>
|                               href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Manual_of_Style/Dates_and_numbers#Chronological_items"
|                               rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                               title="Wikipedia:Manual of Style/Dates and numbers"
|                               <span>
|                                 title="The time period mentioned near this tag is ambiguous. (March 2022)"
|                                 "when?"
|                           <span>
|                             typeof="mw:Entity"
|                             "]"
|                         " HTML specifications lies in the distinction between the SGML-based specification and the XML-based specification. The XML-based specification is usually called "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XHTML"
|                           id="mwBjw"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="XHTML"
|                           "XHTML"
|                         " to distinguish it clearly from the more traditional definition. However, the root element name continues to be "html" even in the XHTML-specified HTML. The W3C intended XHTML 1.0 to be identical to HTML 4.01 except where limitations of XML over the more complex SGML require workarounds. Because XHTML and HTML are closely related, they are sometimes documented in parallel. In such circumstances, some authors "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/(X)HTML"
|                           id="mwBj0"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="(X)HTML"
|                           "conflate the two names"
|                         " as (X)HTML or X(HTML)."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBj4"
|                         "Like HTML 4.01, XHTML 1.0 has three sub-specifications: strict, transitional, and frameset."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBj8"
|                         "Aside from the different opening declarations for a document, the differences between an HTML 4.01 and XHTML 1.0 document—in each of the corresponding DTDs—are largely syntactic. The underlying syntax of HTML allows many shortcuts that XHTML does not, such as elements with optional opening or closing tags, and even empty elements which must not have an end tag. By contrast, XHTML requires all elements to have an opening tag and a closing tag. XHTML, however, also introduces a new shortcut: an XHTML tag may be opened and closed within the same tag, by including a slash before the end of the tag like this: "
|                         <code>
|                           about="#mwt581"
|                           class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br/>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br/>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           dir="ltr"
|                           id="mwBkA"
|                           style=""
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBkE"
|                             "<"
|                           <span>
|                             class="nt"
|                             id="mwBkI"
|                             "br"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBkM"
|                             "/>"
|                         ". The introduction of this shorthand, which is not used in the SGML declaration for HTML 4.01, may confuse earlier software unfamiliar with this new convention. A fix for this is remove the slash preceding the closing angle bracket, as such: "
|                         <code>
|                           about="#mwt583"
|                           class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           dir="ltr"
|                           id="mwBkQ"
|                           style=""
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBkU"
|                             "<"
|                           <span>
|                             class="nt"
|                             id="mwBkY"
|                             "br"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBkc"
|                             ">"
|                         "."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt587"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-98"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-98"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-98"
|                             id="mwBkg"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBkk"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBko"
|                                 "["
|                               "97"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBks"
|                                 "]"
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBkw"
|                         "To understand the subtle differences between HTML and XHTML, consider the transformation of a valid and well-formed XHTML 1.0 document that adheres to Appendix C (see below) into a valid HTML 4.01 document. Making this translation requires the following steps:"
|                       "
"
|                       <ol>
|                         id="mwBk0"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBk4"
|                           "The language for an element is specified with a "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBk8"
|                             "lang"
|                           " attribute rather than the XHTML "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBlA"
|                             "xml:lang"
|                           " attribute. XHTML uses XML's built-in language-defining functionality attribute."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBlE"
|                           "Remove the XML namespace ("
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBlI"
|                             "xmlns=URI"
|                           "). HTML has no facilities for namespaces."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBlM"
|                           "Change the document type declaration from XHTML 1.0 to HTML 4.01."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBlQ"
|                           "If present, remove the XML declaration. Typically this is: "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt588"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-xml mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"xml","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"xml"},"code":{"wt":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBlU"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cp"
|                               id="mwBlY"
|                               "<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>"
|                           "."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBlc"
|                           "Ensure that the document's MIME type is set to "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBlg"
|                             "text/html"
|                           ". For both HTML and XHTML, this comes from the HTTP "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBlk"
|                             "Content-Type"
|                           " header sent by the server."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBlo"
|                           "Change the XML empty-element syntax to an HTML style empty element ("
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt590"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br/>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br/>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBls"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBlw"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBl0"
|                               "br"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBl4"
|                               "/>"
|                           " to "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt592"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBl8"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBmA"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBmE"
|                               "br"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBmI"
|                               ">"
|                           ")."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBmM"
|                         "Those are the main changes necessary to translate a document from XHTML 1.0 to HTML 4.01. To translate from HTML to XHTML would also require the addition of any omitted opening or closing tags. Whether coding in HTML or XHTML it may just be best to always include the optional tags within an HTML document rather than remembering which tags can be omitted."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBmQ"
|                         "A well-formed XHTML document adheres to all the syntax requirements of XML. A valid document adheres to the content specification for XHTML, which describes the document structure."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBmU"
|                         "The W3C recommends several conventions to ensure an easy migration between HTML and XHTML."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt596"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-99"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-99"
|                             id="mwBmY"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBmc"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBmg"
|                                 "["
|                               "98"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBmk"
|                                 "]"
|                         " The following steps can be applied to XHTML 1.0 documents only:"
|                       "
"
|                       <ul>
|                         id="mwBmo"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBms"
|                           "Include both "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBmw"
|                             "xml:lang"
|                           " and "
|                           <code>
|                             id="mwBm0"
|                             "lang"
|                           " attributes on any elements assigning language."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBm4"
|                           "Use the empty-element syntax only for elements specified as empty in HTML."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBm8"
|                           "Remove the closing slash in empty-element tags: for example "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt597"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBnA"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBnE"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBnI"
|                               "br"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBnM"
|                               ">"
|                           " instead of "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt599"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<br/>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<br/>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBnQ"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBnU"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBnY"
|                               "br"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBnc"
|                               "/>"
|                           "."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBng"
|                           "Include explicit close tags for elements that permit content but are left empty (for example, "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt601"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":""}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBnk"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                           ", not "
|                           <code>
|                             about="#mwt603"
|                             class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                             data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<div />"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<div />"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                             dir="ltr"
|                             id="mwBno"
|                             style=""
|                             typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBns"
|                               "<"
|                             <span>
|                               class="nt"
|                               id="mwBnw"
|                               "div"
|                             " "
|                             <span>
|                               class="p"
|                               id="mwBn0"
|                               "/>"
|                           ")."
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBn4"
|                           "Omit the XML declaration."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBn8"
|                         "By carefully following the W3C's compatibility guidelines, a user agent should be able to interpret the document equally as HTML or XHTML. For documents that are XHTML 1.0 and have been made compatible in this way, the W3C permits them to be served either as HTML (with a "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBoA"
|                           "text/html"
|                         " "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIME_type"
|                           id="mwBoE"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="MIME type"
|                           "MIME type"
|                         "), or as XHTML (with an "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBoI"
|                           "application/xhtml+xml"
|                         " or "
|                         <code>
|                           id="mwBoM"
|                           "application/xml"
|                         " MIME type). When delivered as XHTML, browsers should use an XML parser, which adheres strictly to the XML specifications for parsing the document's contents."
|                       "

"
|                     <section>
|                       aria-labelledby="Transitional_versus_strict"
|                       data-mw-section-id="31"
|                       id="mwBoQ"
|                       <div>
|                         class="mw-heading mw-heading3"
|                         <h3>
|                           id="Transitional_versus_strict"
|                           "Transitional versus strict"
|                       "
"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBoU"
|                         "HTML 4 defined three different versions of the language: Strict, Transitional (once called Loose), and Frameset. The Strict version is intended for new documents and is considered best practice, while the Transitional and Frameset versions were developed to make it easier to transition documents that conformed to older HTML specifications or did not conform to any specification to a version of HTML 4. The Transitional and Frameset versions allow for presentational markup, which is omitted in the Strict version. Instead, "
|                         <a>
|                           class="mw-redirect"
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascading_style_sheets"
|                           id="mwBoY"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Cascading style sheets"
|                           "cascading style sheets"
|                         " are encouraged to improve the presentation of HTML documents. Because XHTML 1 only defines an XML syntax for the language defined by HTML 4, the same differences apply to XHTML 1 as well."
|                       "

"
|                       <p>
|                         id="mwBoc"
|                         "The Transitional version allows the following parts of the vocabulary, which are not included in the Strict version:"
|                       "
"
|                       <ul>
|                         id="mwBog"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBok"
|                           "A looser content model
"
|                           <ul>
|                             id="mwBoo"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBos"
|                               "Inline elements and plain text are allowed directly in: "
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBow"
|                                 "body"
|                               ", "
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBo0"
|                                 "blockquote"
|                               ", "
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBo4"
|                                 "form"
|                               ", "
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBo8"
|                                 "noscript"
|                               " and "
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpA"
|                                 "noframes"
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBpE"
|                           "Presentation related elements
"
|                           <ul>
|                             id="mwBpI"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBpM"
|                               "underline ("
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpQ"
|                                 "u"
|                               ") (Deprecated. can confuse a visitor with a hyperlink.)"
|                             "
"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBpU"
|                               "strike-through ("
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpY"
|                                 "s"
|                               ")"
|                             "
"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBpc"
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpg"
|                                 "center"
|                               " (Deprecated. use CSS instead.)"
|                             "
"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBpk"
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpo"
|                                 "font"
|                               " (Deprecated. use CSS instead.)"
|                             "
"
|                             <li>
|                               id="mwBps"
|                               <code>
|                                 id="mwBpw"
|                                 "basefont"
|                               " (Deprecated. use CSS instead.)"
|                         "
"
|                         <li>
|                           id="mwBp0"
|                           "Presentation related attributes
"
|                           <ul>
