|                         rel="mw:PageProp/Category"
|                     "
"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBxc"
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WYSIWYG"
|                         id="mwBxg"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="WYSIWYG"
|                         "WYSIWYG"
|                       " editors ("
|                       <i>
|                         id="mwBxk"
|                         "what you see is what you get"
|                       "), are HTML editors in which the user lays out everything as it is to appear in the HTML document using a "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphical_user_interface"
|                         id="mwBxo"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Graphical user interface"
|                         "graphical user interface"
|                       " (GUI), such as "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_FrontPage"
|                         id="mwBxs"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Microsoft FrontPage"
|                         "Microsoft FrontPage"
|                       ", often similar to "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word_processor"
|                         id="mwBxw"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="Word processor"
|                         "word processors"
|                       ". The editor renders the document rather than showing the code, so authors do not require extensive knowledge of HTML."
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwBx0"
|                       "The WYSIWYG editing model has been criticized,"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt610"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-100"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-100"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-100"
|                           id="mwBx4"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwBx8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwByA"
|                               "["
|                             "99"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwByE"
|                               "]"
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt611"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-101"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-101"
|                           id="mwByI"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwByM"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwByQ"
|                               "["
|                             "100"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwByU"
|                               "]"
|                       " primarily because of the low quality of the generated code; there are various developers advocating a change to the "
|                       <a>
|                         href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WYSIWYM"
|                         id="mwByY"
|                         rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                         title="WYSIWYM"
|                         "WYSIWYM"
|                       " model ("
|                       <i>
|                         id="mwByc"
|                         "what you see is what you mean"
|                       ")."
|                       <sup>
|                         about="#mwt614"
|                         class="mw-ref reference"
|                         data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-102"}}"
|                         id="cite_ref-102"
|                         rel="dc:references"
|                         typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                         <a>
|                           href="#cite_note-102"
|                           id="mwByg"
|                           <span>
|                             class="mw-reflink-text"
|                             id="mwByk"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwByo"
|                               "["
|                             "101"
|                             <span>
|                               class="cite-bracket"
|                               id="mwBys"
|                               "]"
|                     "

"
|                     <p>
|                       id="mwByw"
|                       "WYSIWYG editors remain a controversial topic because of their perceived flaws such as:"
|                     "
"
|                     <ul>
|                       id="mwBy0"
|                       <li>
|                         id="mwBy4"
|                         "Relying mainly on the layout as opposed to meaning, often using markup that does not convey the intended meaning but simply copies the layout."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt616"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-103"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-103"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-103"
|                             id="mwBy8"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBzA"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBzE"
|                                 "["
|                               "102"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBzI"
|                                 "]"
|                       "
"
|                       <li>
|                         id="mwBzM"
|                         "Often producing extremely verbose and redundant code that fails to make use of the cascading nature of HTML and "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CSS"
|                           id="mwBzQ"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="CSS"
|                           "CSS"
|                         "."
|                       "
"
|                       <li>
|                         id="mwBzU"
|                         "Often producing ungrammatical markup, called "
|                         <a>
|                           href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tag_soup"
|                           id="mwBzY"
|                           rel="mw:WikiLink"
|                           title="Tag soup"
|                           "tag soup"
|                         " or semantically incorrect markup (such as "
|                         <code>
|                           about="#mwt617"
|                           class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-html mw-content-ltr"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"syntaxhighlight","attrs":{"lang":"html","class":"","style":"","inline":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"<em>"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"code","href":"./Template:Code"},"params":{"lang":{"wt":"html"},"code":{"wt":"<em>"}},"i":0}}]}"
|                           dir="ltr"
|                           id="mwBzc"
|                           style=""
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBzg"
|                             "<"
|                           <span>
|                             class="nt"
|                             id="mwBzk"
|                             "em"
|                           <span>
|                             class="p"
|                             id="mwBzo"
|                             ">"
|                         " for italics)."
|                       "
"
|                       <li>
|                         id="mwBzs"
|                         "As a great deal of the information in HTML documents is not in the layout, the model has been criticized for its "what you see is all you get"-nature."
|                         <sup>
|                           about="#mwt620"
|                           class="mw-ref reference"
|                           data-mw="{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104"}}"
|                           id="cite_ref-104"
|                           rel="dc:references"
|                           typeof="mw:Extension/ref"
|                           <a>
|                             href="#cite_note-104"
|                             id="mwBzw"
|                             <span>
|                               class="mw-reflink-text"
|                               id="mwBz0"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBz4"
|                                 "["
|                               "103"
|                               <span>
|                                 class="cite-bracket"
|                                 id="mwBz8"
|                                 "]"
|                     "

"
